Z||000005||Seanh||10-10-2000||09:49 PM||||I had my spoiler stolen once. I get my tire valve covers stolen at least once a month. If somone cant even afford tire valve covers, then they shouldn't even have a car in the first place. But now I have a FirstTech 16 Channel Security System on my baby, if anyone so much as spits on my car the whole neighbor hood will know, and the remote transmitter will be paged up to 2 miles away. I still can keep those damn tire valve covers on though. Perhaps if I get some metal ones, leave my car out a couple of days with a 15K volt transfomer on them, and just wait for the scream?<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000006||Supernaut||10-11-2000||10:17 AM||||I got hit too, Monday night/Tuesday morning.  They poked all four tires flat and put a cinderblock through the windshield of my '84 beater/now parts car.  They tried to pop the side windows as well, but looks like Pontiac glass was tougher than masonary.  I'm just glad they didn't get to the silver shadow in the garage during this orgy of destruction.<P>Two encouraging points though...the police told me that they have a very good idea as to the identity of the perpetrators...secondly, after closer inspection it appears that one of them made the tragic mistake of hurling a cinderblock down on the hood at high velocity while not taking into consideration the tendancy of the plastic body panels to hurl back instead of simply absorbing the impact - looks like he caught it in the nose, judging from the blotchy trail of blood that seems to stagger away from the car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>poor bastard...hehehehe<P>------------------<BR>Supernaut<BR>86 GT (in progress)<BR>86 SE<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/signat.gif"> ||||reg||8
