Z||000008||Raydar||10-11-2000||05:07 PM||||A guy that I knew a few years back, came out of school one day and saw someone sitting in his car, door open, feet on the ground, head under the dash, trying to hotwire it, or get the stereo. He went running up to the door, and threw all his weight (about 225 lbs) against it. Needless to say the person *did not* get up and run away. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||10-11-2000||05:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>A guy that I knew a few years back, came out of school one day and saw someone sitting in his car, door open, feet on the ground, head under the dash, trying to hotwire it, or get the stereo. He went running up to the door, and threw all his weight (about 225 lbs) against it. Needless to say the person *did not* get up and run away. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In Canada you'd probably get arrested for that, and then the thief would sue you or some cr@p like that.. you're not allowed to defend your property here.. and sometimes you're not allowed to defend yourself even.... the laws here suck sometimes.<P>loved the story though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000010||loafer87gt||10-11-2000||05:34 PM||||I just leave my Fiero back at my acreage in the country while I'm going to college in the city of Saskatoon. I have had my car stolen once, and broken into twice in front of my house during the past year and a half. Like Darklord said, in Canada you don't dare do anything to a thief if you catch him breaking into your car, or else you'll get charged with assault or accused of being a racist. I was so pissed last time my car was broken into: the guy smashed the side window of the car, but cut his arm fairly badly badly as there was blood all over the inside of the car. I called the police to see if they could take a blood sample and use it to help try and nail the kid down the street (who is on house arrest for stealing several computers from the university, and I saw a car EXACTLY like his stop and check out my car two nights before, which I reported to the police) and I was told that is against the criminals rights. Apparently in Canada, you cannot use any DNA evidence unless the person did you physical harm. What a load of BS! In my opinion, the person did do me physical harm, I had to work several extra hours of OT to help pay for the damages to my car, and was without a ride for 2 months while the work was being done! Things are so stupid up here that a guy in the city went to kick in a window at a pawn shop, and cut the tendons out of the back of his knee. He managed to succesfully sue the store owner for damages. Just plain crazy if you ask me.||||reg||1
