Z||000015||Raydar||10-12-2000||09:45 AM||||I've heard about the "no rights for the victim" situation in Canada. It's not quite that bad in the US, but some folks are trying to make it so. <BR>If someone breaks into your home or jumps into your car, or does anything <I>that puts you in fear of your life</I>, then in the eyes of the law you are pretty much justified in whatever you need to do to protect yourself.<BR>Contrary to the "official" position, most police officers will tell you that the "average" person <I>should</I> own a gun, and know how to use it. <BR>Regarding the previous statements, if you shoot somebody, you <I>had better</I> have a "carry" permit (unless you're in your home).<P>BTW... That situation with my friend in the school parking lot happened over 20 years ago. (Damn I feel old.) <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||frontal lobe||10-12-2000||10:26 AM||||Oh Canada,<BR>Glorious and free,<BR>Oh Canada,<BR>We stand on guard for thee.<BR>Oh Canada,<BR>We stand on guard for thee.<P>But we don't let you stand on guard for your cars or other property.<P>Who would you be accused of being racist against for defending your property--french people?????<P>I'm just joking.  I like your national anthem--musically better than mine.  And seriously, racist against who?||||reg||1
Z||000017||loafer87gt||10-12-2000||12:44 PM||||Frontal Lobe: There is a lot of tension between the natives in the city and the police officers. There is an old power generator about a block and a half outside of the city that police officers take intoxicated people to sober up on the walk home, and last year, a native was found frozen on the outskirts of town. Two police officers have been removed from the force, and there is an ongoing investigation into racist practices in the city. The police in the town now have to be very carefull when dealing with the natives, or could end up getting caught up in the going ons.||||reg||1
Z||000018||frontal lobe||10-12-2000||02:12 PM||||loafer87gt,<P>Oh.  I didn't realize the natives (native indians, right) were persecuted in Canada.  In Wisconsin, where I live, we are careful to protect their right to live their culture the way they have for centuries:  running gambling casinos!  Also, the state is considering removing the name "Squaw" from all towns, lakes, etc.<P>Interesting world we live in.  Sorry I got so far off topic.||||reg||1
